+++
{{ if .Example -}}
# A plan holds the documents, milestones, and contracts that pursue one goal. Copy this file to
# plan/plan.md. Approving a version of the plan approves every document version it lists, records its
# draft decisions as the approving member's decisions, and passes the contract review of its work.
{{ else -}}
# A plan holds the documents, milestones, and contracts that pursue one goal. Approving a version of the
# plan approves every document version it lists, records its draft decisions as the approving member's
# decisions, and passes the contract review of its work.
{{ end -}}
kind = "plan"
# The plan's ID names the plan, not a version. Ropeshift numbers each committed change as a new version
# of the same plan. A later plan for another goal gets an ID of its own, such as {{ .Project }}-v2.
id = "{{ .Project }}-v1"
{{ if .Example -}}
title = "Self-service accounts"
# The id of the goal file.
goal = "self-service-accounts"
# Every document the plan holds, as kind:id. A listed document must exist, so remove the entries for
# the templates you do not copy. Contracts are not listed: each names this plan in its `plan` key.
documents = [
  "requirements:acme-accounts",
  "spec:accounts-endpoints",
  "architecture:acme-accounts",
  "experience-design:account-settings",
  "milestone:m1-accounts",
  "repositories:acme",
]

# A draft decision records an answer the person gave while planning. It binds nothing until the plan is
# approved. A planning session writes these from the conversation; a plan written by hand usually has none.
[[decision]]
id = "d1"
question = "Does a new email address take effect before the customer confirms it?"
answer = "No. It takes effect once the customer follows the link sent to the new address."
rationale = "An unconfirmed address could lock the customer out of account recovery."
# true holds the plan's approval while the question behind it is still open.
blocking = false

# An adoption records each branch, pull request, or issue the plan does not carry, as branch:<name>,
# pull:<number>, or issue:<id>, with the reason, so approval shows it.
# [[left_out]]
# ref = "branch:spike/old-settings"
# reason = "An experiment the team abandoned"
{{ else -}}
title = "State the plan in one line"
# The id of the goal file.
goal = "{{ .Project }}-goal"
# Every document the plan holds, as kind:id. A listed document must exist, so add an entry for each
# document you write. Contracts are not listed: each names this plan in its `plan` key.
documents = [
  "requirements:{{ .Project }}-requirements",
{{- if .Repositories }}
  "repositories:{{ .Project }}",
{{- end }}
]
{{ end -}}
+++

How the work is planned, in prose: the order of the milestones, the shared contracts built first, and what
the plan leaves for later.
